piece acidhouse
bpm 128
bars 64

# Two minutes of acid under offbeat stabs, which is the blueprint for a whole
# genre and the two things that worked on the bench.
#
#   bars  1-8   kick alone, then hats. Getting your bearings
#   bars  9-16  clap and sub. The groove
#   bars 17-24  the acid, filter shut and opening across eight bars
#   bars 25-32  stabs join it. The first full bar of the track
#   bars 33-40  THE BREAKDOWN. Drums out. The stabs stop chopping and hold;
#               the acid drops to a mutter under them
#   bars 41-48  the build. Kick back, the acid climbing, the clap returning
#   bars 49-56  the drop. Everything, filter wide, the stabs biting again
#   bars 57-64  out. The kit goes first, the acid last
#
# The stages are macros, which the tab format could not say until today. An
# acid line is a filter and a resonance and almost nothing else, so a static
# one is a loop and a swept one is an arrangement — the difference between
# eight bars of the same thing and eight bars that go somewhere.

# Everything 0.84x: the mix reached -0.03 dBFS, which is no headroom at all.
lane kick  clip=floor inst=kick root=A1  gain=0.798 len=0.4s
lane clap  clip=floor inst=hat  root=C-1 gain=0.462 len=0.16s send=0.35
lane hat   clip=floor inst=hat  root=C-1 gain=0.252 len=0.04s send=0.08 orbit=1.1/8/0/0/0/1
lane sub   clip=floor inst=bass root=A0  gain=0.672 len=1.6 duck

lane acid  clip=hook inst=bass    root=A1 gain=0.714 len=0.9 duck vel=8
lane stab1 clip=hook inst=strings root=A2 gain=1.302 len=1.6 send=0.3 vel=8
lane stab2 clip=hook inst=strings root=A2 gain=1.159 len=1.6 send=0.3 vel=8
lane stab3 clip=hook inst=strings root=A2 gain=1.092 len=1.6 send=0.35 vel=8

grid floor bars 1-64
